  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "parent": "FS-QUERY-INDEX",
  "parentStatus": "IMPLEMENTING",
  "oracleTrack": "disposable-sandbox",
  "oracle": {
    "project": "fireemu-oracle-query",
    "database": "(default)",
    "edition": "STANDARD",
    "location": "us-central1",
    "indexes": "conformance/fs-query-index.indexes.json"
  },
  "closureReview": {
    "decision": "PENDING"
  },
  "scopeDecisions": [
    {
      "id": "Q1",
      "decision": "The whole corpus is observed over REST v1; representative cases of every surface are also observed over gRPC google.firestore.v1. Client SDK paths (limitToLast reversal, listeners, caches) belong to FS-LISTEN-SDK.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-LISTEN-SDK"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2",
      "decision": "The sandbox (default) database carries the lane superset conformance/fs-query-index.indexes.json (the shared conformance/firestore.indexes.json plus lane-only collection groups). The shared file stays unchanged because other campaigns bind its digest.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q3",
      "decision": "Under the strict profile a missing-index refusal matches production exactly, console link and encoded index included. The emulator profile keeps its firestore.indexes.json fragment hint and is not closure evidence.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4a",
      "decision": "Vector search (findNearest) on the Standard edition is in scope.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4b",
      "decision": "Pipeline execution semantics stay FS-ENTERPRISE-EXCLUDED; the Standard-edition refusal of ExecutePipeline is production behavior and is in scope.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-ENTERPRISE-EXCLUDED"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4c",
      "decision": "Index and field administration methods (collectionGroups.indexes.*, collectionGroups.fields.*) that the API denominator assigns here belong to FS-CONFIG-LIFECYCLE; Listen target types (QueryTarget, BloomFilter, ExistenceFilter) belong to FS-LISTEN-SDK.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-CONFIG-LIFECYCLE"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4d",
      "decision": "Read times on runQuery, runAggregationQuery and partitionQuery are observed here; queries inside transactions and transaction options stay in FS-TRANSACTION.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-TRANSACTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "decision": "Closure evidence is the sandbox re-record. Historical production evidence (the 2026-09-07 matrix query rows, the aggregation corpora, the Explain v5 receipt and the 2026-09-08 index-merge check) corroborates it and stays immutable. The historical 324-row regression belongs to FS-DATA-WRITE, as do listDocuments, listCollectionIds and the index-entry write limits.",
      "decidedBy": "lane agent, following the parent table and the AUTH-ACCOUNT precedent; confirmed at closure review",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-DATA-WRITE"
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "decision": "Zero gap: response bodies, including error message text, must equal production after normalization. A documented divergence needs an owner decision naming the row.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (standing zero-gap directive of 2026-09-18)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-18"
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "decision": "Rules-based query authorization belongs to FS-RULES; this corpus runs with owner credentials.",
      "decidedBy": "lane agent, following the parent table and the AUTH-ACCOUNT precedent; confirmed at closure review",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-RULES"
    },
    {
      "id": "S4",
      "decision": "Documented divergence: production lists a set of field paths in the order of an internal hash set, in the 'distinct inequality fields: [...]' refusal and in the member order of an index merge in Explain planSummary (which also sets the order the merge walks its members, and so index_entries_scanned). The order is stable across recordings but no standard container or hash reproduces it (about 45 families tested, linear hashes ruled out by proof). fireemu lists inequality fields in field-path order and merge members in planning order. The comparison treats these lists as unordered, and the merge entry count as masked, on the named rows only (conformance/src/fs-query-index/divergences.mjs); everything else in those rows is compared strictly and the raw recordings are unchanged.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "S5",
      "decision": "Documented divergence: production chooses PartitionQuery cursors at keys sampled by an internal hash that could not be recovered (docs.local candidate tournament, GF(2) proof against linear and CRC families). fireemu reproduces the structure: about one key in 141 is a sample, partition_count cursors (every sample when there are fewer) nested across counts, in key order, without before, with production's paging, tokens and refusals; it samples with its own stable hash, so the keys differ. The comparison masks the cursor keys (their number and shape stay strict), accepts fewer cursors than requested as every sample on the count-64 row, and masks the four range counts while requiring that they add up to the same total on both sides, on the named rows only.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    }
  ],
